<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48747" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Trans-alpīnus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>that is</i> or <i>lies beyond the
			Alps</i>, <i>Transalpine</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Gallia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Caes. B.
					G. 7, 1</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">7, 6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. Mur. 41, 89</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cognatio materna Transalpini sanguinis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Red. in Sen. 7, 15</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nationes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Fam. 9, 15, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bella,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Off. 2, 8, 28</span></i>
			.—In <i>plur. subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Transalpīni</span></b> ,
				ōrum, m., <i>nations beyond the Alps</i>, <i>Transalpine
				nations</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">legio una ex Transalpinis conscripta,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Caes. 24</span></i>
			.</div>
